</html>

<style>
  /* Every colour here is a bridge token. `apps/support` has no `--color-*` vocabulary — the portal's
     palette is `--bo-*`, declared once in `brand/baseout-bridge.css` and worn by four public apps.
     Spacing is on the 4px grid throughout; the two 1px values are borders. */
  :global(html) {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bo-root-bg);
    color: var(--bo-base-content);
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  :global(*) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .hf {
    /* 82.5rem = 1320px, the width `apps/design/src/pages/handoff.astro` uses. The arithmetic that
       makes the rail fit is on `.hf-layout` below. */
    max-width: 82.5rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 32px 24px 96px;
  }

  /* ── Header ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hf-eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }
  .hf-h1 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 32px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .hf-lede {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 46rem;
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
  }
  .hf-lede code {
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .hf-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .hf-count {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  /* ── The rail, the search, and what both become when the rail has nowhere to stand ────────────

     THE ARITHMETIC, at 1440 and stated because the last two rulings about this row were made without
     it and both were wrong:

         .hf max-width          1320   (82.5rem — the app's handoff, matched deliberately)
         horizontal padding     24 + 24
         inner                  1272
         rail track             212
         column gap             40
         content track          1020   = 1272 − 212 − 40

     1152 was the old measure and it is what made a rail "impossible": 1152 centred leaves 144px
     gutters, and a rail of full-width labels needs about 168 (the widest label, `Cross-cutting`,
     measured 132 as a chip, plus a count badge and padding). The gutter was never the place. The
     column is — and 1020 is still wider than the 62ch every lede on this page is capped at, so
     nothing readable got narrower. It also lands exactly on what the emails section needs: a 600px
     frame, a 24px gap and a 396px notes column.

     WHAT IT BECOMES AS THE VIEWPORT NARROWS. Content = min(vw, 1320) − 48 − 252. At 1160 that is
     860; below it the content column starts eating the reading measure, so 1160 is the switch — the
     same breakpoint the app uses. Under it the rail goes back to being exactly what this page had
     before: one horizontal row of chips above the content, sticky, its own scroller at 390 rather
     than four wrapped rows eating a third of the viewport. The sub-rows do NOT flatten into that
     row: ten chips is a row you can read and thirty is not, so at narrow widths they appear only
     while the search is showing them.

     `--hf-nav-mode` IS HOW THE SCRIPT KNOWS WHICH ONE IT IS. The breakpoint lives here, in CSS, and
     `lib/handoff.ts` reads the answer rather than re-deriving it from a width it would then own a
     second copy of. It decides two things: what `--hf-nav-h` is (a rail covers nothing, so 0; a bar
     covers its own height) and where the scroll-spy's reading line sits. */

  .hf-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 212px;
    column-gap: 40px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .hf-head {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .hf-rail {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 1 / span 2;
    position: sticky;
    top: 16px;
    align-self: start;
    max-height: calc(100vh - 32px);
    overflow-y: auto;
    scrollbar-width: thin;
    --hf-nav-mode: rail;
  }
  .hf-body {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 2;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .hf-toc {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  /* Every child of a flex box gets its margin reset here rather than trusted: a general-sibling
     prose rule reaches into nested flex and grid boxes in this app, and it has already produced one
     crooked row and one wrong card gap. */
  .hf-toc > *,
  .hf-toc-grp > *,
  .hf-subnav > * {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .hf-toc-h {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 8px 8px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }
  .hf-toc-grp {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  .hf-nav-a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border-left: 2px solid transparent;
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
    font-size: 13px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .hf-nav-a-t {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .hf-nav-a:hover {
    background: var(--bo-base-100);
    color: var(--bo-primary);
  }
  /* WHERE THE READER IS. `aria-current` rather than a class, because the state is the same fact for
     the screen reader and for the eye, and carrying it twice is how the two drift apart. */
  .hf-nav-a[aria-current='true'] {
    background: var(--bo-soft-primary-bg);
    color: var(--bo-soft-primary-fg);
    border-left-color: var(--bo-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* THE COUNT IS WHAT MAKES IT AN INDEX. A developer reads `Tickets 5` and knows the size of what
     they are about to open; a menu row tells them only that it exists. */
  .hf-n {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    padding: 0 8px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--bo-base-200);
    color: var(--bo-muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 20px;
  }
  .hf-subnav {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    margin: 4px 0 4px 12px;
    padding-left: 8px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
  }
  .hf-nav-a.hf-sub {
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-left: 0;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .hf-nav-act {
    display: flex;
    gap: 4px;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .hf-nav-btn {
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bo-base-100);
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .hf-nav-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--bo-primary);
    color: var(--bo-primary);
  }

  /* ── The search, in the content column ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .hf-find {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bo-base-100);
  }
  .hf-find > * {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .hf-find:focus-within {
    border-color: var(--bo-primary);
  }
  .hf-find .bo-i {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }
  .hf-find-input {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--bo-base-content);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .hf-find-input:focus {
    outline: none;
  }
  .hf-find-n {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }
  .hf-find-none {
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }
  .hf-find-clear {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--bo-primary);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
    text-decoration: underline;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* ONE HIDING MECHANISM FOR THE WHOLE FILTER, and it is an attribute rather than `hidden`: an
     author `display` beats that attribute, and this app has shipped that defect once already. */
  /* `:global()` IS LOAD BEARING. A scoped selector compiles to `[data-hf-hide='true'].astro-<page>`
     and the emails section is emitted by a CHILD COMPONENT, which carries its own hash — so without
     this the filter would hide every flow on the page and leave the three email cards on screen,
     with every gate green. Same defect as the one recorded in `components/HandoffEmails.astro`. */
  :global([data-hf-hide='true']) {
    display: none;
  }

  /* ── Narrow: the rail becomes the chip bar this page already had ────────── */
  @media (max-width: 1160px) {
    .hf-layout {
      display: block;
    }
    .hf-rail {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 20;
      max-height: none;
      overflow: visible;
      margin: 0 -24px 20px;
      padding: 8px 24px;
      background: var(--bo-root-bg);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
      --hf-nav-mode: bar;
    }
    .hf-toc {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      /* ONE ROW THAT SCROLLS, NEVER FOUR THAT WRAP. Ten chips wrapped at 390 would be a third of the
         viewport permanently pinned to the top, which is the failure this control exists to avoid. */
      overflow-x: auto;
      overflow-y: hidden;
      scrollbar-width: thin;
      padding: 4px 0;
    }
    .hf-toc-h {
      display: none;
    }
    /* The group wrapper dissolves so its row and its sub-rows sit directly in the chip row. */
    .hf-toc-grp {
      display: contents;
    }
    .hf-nav-a {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
      border-left-width: 1px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--bo-base-100);
      color: var(--bo-base-content);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .hf-nav-a[aria-current='true'] {
      border-color: transparent;
    }
    .hf-nav-a-t {
      overflow: visible;
      text-overflow: clip;
    }
    /* The counts leave the chips. Ten chips already need more room than the row has at 1160, and a
       badge on each is 28px it does not have; the count is an index affordance and the bar is not an
       index. */
    .hf-n {
      display: none;
    }
    .hf-subnav {
      display: contents;
    }
    .hf-rail {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
    }
    .hf-toc {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-width: 0;
    }
    .hf-nav-act {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }

  /* ── The one badge axis ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* BUILT OR NOT BUILT, AND NOTHING ELSE WEARS A COLOUR. The page carried 407 badges in two
     competing taxonomies — a probe name on every edge row and a severity beside it — and the
     complaint was that it all ran together. Everything that used to be a chip is now either a
     sentence or a plain count in muted text: a number a reader can read is worth more than a colour
     they have to decode. Soft background, semantic foreground, never outline. */
  .hf-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .hf-pill[data-built='true'] {
    background: var(--bo-soft-success-bg);
    color: var(--bo-soft-success-fg);
  }
  .hf-pill[data-built='false'] {
    background: var(--bo-soft-warning-bg);
    color: var(--bo-soft-warning-fg);
  }

  /* ── Surface groups ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hf-surface {
    margin-top: 40px;
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--hf-nav-h, 56px) + 16px);
  }
  .hf-h2 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .hf-h2-n {
    margin-left: auto;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  .hf-flows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  /* ── A FLOW IS CLOSED UNTIL SOMEBODY OPENS IT ───────────────────────────── */
  /* A closed row still carries everything that decides whether to open it: whether it is built, how
     many of its states you can open, how many things are wrong in it, and whether its steps are a
     sequence or the states of one screen. Native `<details>`, so it works with no JavaScript, takes
     keyboard focus for free, and is what Ctrl+F expands in browsers that support find-in-page
     through closed details. */
  .hf-flow {
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--bo-base-100);
    padding: 12px 20px;
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--hf-nav-h, 56px) + 16px);
  }
  .hf-flow[open] {
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .hf-flow-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .hf-flow-head::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .hf-flow-head:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--bo-primary);
    outline-offset: 4px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .hf-flow-chev {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
    transition: transform 120ms ease;
  }
  .hf-flow[open] .hf-flow-chev {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hf-flow-chev {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
  .hf-flow-title {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 4px 8px;
    min-width: 0;
    margin-right: auto;
  }
  .hf-h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .hf-flow-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  /* A COUNT IS A WORD, NOT A TAXONOMY. `2 things wrong here` needs no legend; a red chip does. */
  .hf-completeness {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }
  .hf-completeness[data-shape] {
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ── 1 · What happens here ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hf-what {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    max-width: 46rem;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--bo-base-content);
  }

  /* ── 2 · The states you can open ────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* WHERE THE STEPS ARE THE STATES OF ONE SCREEN, THEY GO ON ONE ROW. Signed out · The list · Open ·
     Closed · All · Never written in is one feature seen six ways, and stacking it as six full-width
     numbered cards says it is six things that happen in order. The registry decides which flows get
     this (`HandoffShape`). */
  .hf-chips {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .hf-chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--bo-soft-primary-bg);
    color: var(--bo-soft-primary-fg);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .hf-chip:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  /* A STATE WITH NO ADDRESS DOES NOT GET A LINK, AND SAYS WHY. It is drawn as the same chip without
     the plate, so the row still reads as one set — the difference is that one is clickable and one
     tells you why it is not. */
  .hf-chip[data-nolink] {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
    border: 1px dashed var(--bo-base-300);
  }
  .hf-chip-why {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* A REAL SEQUENCE STAYS NUMBERED AND IN ORDER, because step 3 is only reachable by having done
     step 2. Drawing it as an unordered row of chips would destroy that. */
  .hf-seq {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .hf-step {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 8px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--bo-base-200);
  }
  .hf-step-n {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    margin-top: 2px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--bo-base-200);
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }
  .hf-step[data-kind='not-built'] .hf-step-n {
    background: var(--bo-soft-warning-bg);
    color: var(--bo-soft-warning-fg);
  }
  .hf-step-body {
    min-width: 0;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }
  .hf-step-label {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 4px 8px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .hf-step-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    color: var(--bo-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .hf-step-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .hf-step-caption {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
  }

  /* ── 3 · What is missing or wrong ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* PLAIN SENTENCES, NOT A REGISTER. No probe name, no severity, no `file:line`, no id — those are
     the engineer's half and they are in `openspec/changes/support-handoff/edge-register.md`. What
     is left is the sentence a reader could have written after using the thing. */
  .hf-wrong {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bo-base-200);
  }
  .hf-wrong-h {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .hf-wrong ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
  }
  .hf-wrong li {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .hf-wrong-more {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  /* ── Runs through everything ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hf-x {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .hf-x-item {
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--bo-base-100);
    padding: 12px 16px;
  }
  .hf-x-title {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 650;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .hf-x-flows {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 4px 8px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .hf-x-key {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }
  .hf-x-flow {
